[what can you do with scrolls of mail]

By eyeballing the code, you can't turn mail scrolls into blanks by
#dipping or jumping into water, or cancelling them.  If you polymorph
it, it's still a scroll of mail, but if you then read it, it says
it's junk mail from Larn!

It does have a very small monitary base value, but almost worthless.

I still want to add something I should've put in originally; have it
send you 'a scroll of mail named "From: dmr"' (or whoever sent you
the mail), like a return address.

An item which might be in 3.1 (I don't know if the dev. team has decided
to OK it or not) are scrolls of advertising.  You can rarely find them,
but good customers will get them when they buy lots of stuff (but only
one store at most will use them).  It's a teleportation scroll that
'ports you right outside the shop door (even if you're on a different
level).  If you look at the scroll in your inventory, it'll tell you
"VISIT xxx's SHOP ON LEVEL 4", or, on level 4, "YOU ARE ONLY 34 STEPS
AWAY FROM xxx's SHOP", or other advertspeak.  If the store doesn't
exist yet, it says one is opening soon.

